From bf55d17e4d47d9265aaa0c9af7525640e6b504e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2026 12:24:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bifrost: stddev aggregation via per-CPU [n, sum, sum_sq]
 triple
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

W5 partial — stddev() aggregation. The kernel-side reducer
returns the (n, sum, sum_sq) triple; the host renderer computes
sqrt((sum_sq * n - sum²) / (n * (n-1))) at render time. SHMEM
ringbuf wire format extends the per-row agg-snapshot entry shape
from
    i32 fd, u32 k_size, k[k_size], u64 v
to
    i32 fd, u32 k_size, k[k_size], u32 v_size, v[v_size]
so stddev can ship 24-byte (n, sum, sum_sq) triples alongside the
8-byte sum/min/max/avg values. No backward compatibility with V3
hosts (per project directive).

Adds:

- kernel/bpf/syscall.c: bifrost_map_lookup_stddev_u64(map, key,
  *out_n, *out_sum, *out_sum_sq). Sums all three across CPUs
  (value_size=24, [n][sum][sum_sq]). Mirrors avg's structure
  with one extra slot.
- rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h: extern declaration.
- drivers/bifrost/wire.rs: AGG_KIND_STDDEV = 4. Canonical SHA
  pin refreshed.
- drivers/bifrost/agg_snapshot.rs: per-row v_size field;
  STDDEV maps invoke the new reducer and write 24-byte values
  (n, sum, sum_sq); other agg kinds keep writing 8 bytes.

lquantize / llquantize / clear / normalize / trunc remain on
the W5 follow-on punch list in docs/dtrace-roadmap.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
